 "bottom_line": "<p>Snowfall increases significantly as you climb in elevation due to high freezing levels during this storm. At the uppermost elevations, you can trigger avalanches where recent storm snow sits above a weak layer near the surface of the snowpack.</p><p>The most dangerous slopes face north, northeast, and east where winds drift snow onto lee slopes, forming thicker and more connected slabs. As you move down in elevation, avalanches will become smaller and more isolated.</p><p>You can find safer travel options at lower elevations and in wind-sheltered areas.</p>",
